+	// mapsMu protects mappings.
+	mapsMu mapsMutex `state:"nosave"`
+
+	// mappings tracks application mappings of this FD, so that they can be
+	// invalidated by InvalidateUnsavable before saving. Device pmas are not
+	// savable, and a process may hold device mappings that were not removed
+	// by cuda-checkpoint, e.g. mappings inherited across fork(2) by children
+	// that never initialized CUDA (compare CRIU's cuda_plugin, which fails to
+	// dump such processes). Dropping the pmas allows the mappings themselves
+	// to be saved; post-restore accesses fault and re-translate against the
+	// restored host FD (and typically fail, as with fsimpl/host), but this is
+	// only reachable for mappings that cuda-checkpoint did not manage.
+	//
+	// +checklocks:mapsMu
+	mappings memmap.MappingSet
+
